model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The live host protocol's drive history takes an optional note path and returns each commit's server-written time, and a devices query reports the head, the last change time and each device grant's last sync with the head it saw. The host passes the caller it already authenticated to the vault object, which records a device grant's sync from its ordinary listing, change-range and landed-write calls, so no plugin update is needed. Protocols 38 to 40 keep their frozen drive and workflow-step commands. Connect Obsidian links BRAT on its latest track, not the dashboard's version: BRAT freezes any other version and skips it in its startup update, so an install would stay on the version it was connected with."
    }
  }
}
